        <owl:imports rdf:resource="http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/schemas/cpannotationschema.owl"/>
        <terms:description rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Ontology design pattern for modeling smarthome geometry relationships and concepts.</terms:description>
        <terms:title rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">Smarthome Geometry Pattern</terms:title>
        <cpannotationschema:coversRequirements rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">What are the spatial entities (objects with geometry) in a smart home environment?</cpannotationschema:coversRequirements>
        <cpannotationschema:isSpecializationOf rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">This pattern is a spacializayion of the GeoSPARQL ontology (http://www.opengis.net/ont/geosparql) in order to be used in the definition of spatial entities (e.g. places or physical objects) in a smart environment.</cpannotationschema:isSpecializationOf>
        <rdfs:comment xml:lang="en">Curated by OntoBoard 1.155.0, so that the pattern passes ODK&apos;s quality report with its default profile, names every term with a label, and is consistent and coherent. Changes: label added x26; term declared x4;
- header: dcterms:title &quot;Smarthome Geometry Pattern&quot; - the library&apos;s name for the pattern
- header: dcterms:description - the library&apos;s description of the pattern
Each change is listed under &quot;curated&quot; in the pattern&apos;s metadata.json in OntoBoard&apos;s pattern library.</rdfs:comment>
    </owl:Ontology>
    


